Akasan:
{{Short description|Haitian beverage}}
'''Akasan''' (sometimes ''Aka100'') is a popular [[Haiti]]an beverage made from corn kernels, [[Anise|anise stars]], vanilla and cinnamon. It is drunk either warm or cold, often as a breakfast beverage. Akasan is known for its rich sweetness and thickness.<ref>{{cite book|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=AFqkDgG8Nf0C&dq=akasan+%28ak+100%29&pg=PA373 |title=Fine Haitian Cuisine |author=Ménager, Mona Cassion |page=373 |year=2005 |isbn=158432256X |accessdate=12 June 2015}}</ref>

