Punt e Mes:
{{Short description|Italian vermouth}}
[[File:Bottle_of_Punt_E_Mes_vermouth.jpg | thumb | right | A bottle of Punt E Mes]]
'''Punt e Mes''' (from {{langx|pms|pont e mes}} {{IPA|pms|ˈpʊŋt e ˈmez|}}, "[one] point and a half") is an [[Cuisine of Italy|Italian]] [[vermouth]]. It is dark brown in color and has a bitter flavor.  According to its producer, the name refers to the flavor being characterized as half a "point" of [[bitter taste|bitterness]] and one "point" of [[sweetness]].<ref>[http://www.puntemes.it Official site]</ref>

It can be used as a substitute for regular rosso vermouth in such drinks as the [[Americano (cocktail)|Americano]], [[Manhattan (cocktail)|Manhattan]], [[Negroni]], and [[Boulevardier (cocktail)|Boulevardier]]. Punt e Mes has a strong, distinctive flavor, half-way between regular rosso vermouth and [[Campari]]. Punt e Mes was made by the [[Antonio Benedetto Carpano|Carpano]] family from [[Turin]] until 2001, when Distillerie [[Fratelli Branca]] of [[Milan]] bought it.<ref>{{cite news | first=Andrea | last=Ciappi | title=Not Just Fernet | date=May 2005 | url =http://www.chianticlassico.com/english/magazine/200505/articolo1.asp  | work =Chianti Classico Magazine | access-date = 2007-09-18 |archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20070827231933/http://www.chianticlassico.com/english/magazine/200505/articolo1.asp |archive-date = 2007-08-27}}</ref>

