Whisky Mac:
{{Short description|Cocktail with whisky and ginger wine}}
A '''whisky Macdonald''', more commonly known under the shortened name '''whisky Mac''', is a [[cocktail]] made up of [[whisky]] and [[ginger wine]]. The whisky is expected to be a [[Scotch whisky]], usually a blended type. The ginger wine should be green ginger wine. Recipes vary from those having equal parts of each ingredient to those that use a ratio of 3 to 2 of whisky to wine.

A common recipe is to take {{convert|1+1/2|impfloz|mL|abbr=off|round=5|order=flip}} Scotch whisky and {{convert|1+1/2|impfloz|mL|abbr=on|round=5|order=flip}} green ginger wine.<ref>http://www.scotch-whisky.org.uk/swa/233.html {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090607084821/http://www.scotch-whisky.org.uk/swa/233.html |date=2009-06-07 }} "Whisky Mac recipe"</ref> Pour both of the ingredients into a wine goblet with no ice. A hot version can also be made, akin to a [[hot toddy]], made with the addition of boiling water.

The invention of it, and its name, is attributed to Colonel [[Hector MacDonald]], who devised it during the days of the [[British Raj]] in India.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.liquor.com/recipes/whisky-mac/#gs.k4w4es|title=Whisky Mac: Verified Recipe|last=Emen|first=Jake|website=Liquor.com|access-date=5 December 2019}}[http://www.lodge76.wanadoo.co.uk/crabbie%27s.htm] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091210193506/http://www.lodge76.wanadoo.co.uk/crabbie%27s.htm |date=2009-12-10 }}</ref> The mixed drink is sometimes referred to as "The Golfers' Favourite". Apparently, golfers drank whisky macs to ward off the cold after a chilly round on the links.

